  "contract": [
    "Null rows or zero length logs the native buffer error. Otherwise count=(length/12)&255, including quotient wrap; nonzero sub-row lengths produce no rows without that error.",
    "Initialize24-byte header once. Capture each row address before read, reload device/read callback, and compare header words8/12 against live row words4/8 after read. Read status is ignored and partial-read header bytes carry forward.",
    "For matches reload device/write callback and program four-byte11223344 at captured address+20, with unsigned wrap. Only a nonzero write status logs an error; continue later rows regardless.",
    "Each error diagnostic reloads the live row address independently after logging-mode callbacks. Preserve the sole existing12-byte sleep context owner, its section flags/alignment and cold bytes."
  ],
